        "1. Load one MASTER IMAGE. It supplies identity, wardrobe, location and lighting to every Krea2 slide. Its separate planning connection lets the visual model inspect the scene.\n\n2. MASTER AUTO: select Local, Gemini or Grok, choose 1–8 poses and press Prepare pose list. The model examines the master and writes pose, hand-position and framing instructions. A cloud request sends the master image to the selected provider.\n\n3. REVIEW FIRST leaves the generated list editable before Queue carousel. To continue automatically after successful analysis, choose the automatic queue option in After prepare before pressing Prepare. Uploading an image alone never starts an API call or render.\n\n4. REFERENCE COPY: optionally upload pose examples into the Batch Loader, then use Run pose analysis. Choose Simple or Detailed extraction. These images supply poses only; they never replace the Krea2 master.\n\n5. VIBE LIST creates poses from creative direction without needing an image reference. All modes let you review and edit one pose per line.\n\n6. Krea2 always edits the same master with one instruction per active slide. The original 2 MP aspect pipeline, Power LoRA stack and Sage Attention settings are retained. Optional LoRAs start OFF; enable your intended character/style LoRAs and supply their trigger if needed."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
